If a patient has an objective-opioid-withdrawal-sign then every clinician should conduct a standard-buprenorphine-initiation for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-withdrawal-symptom during a standard-buprenorphine-initiation and a buprenorphine-dose-increase is needed for the patient then every clinician should increase a buprenorphine-dose for the patient during the standard-buprenorphine-initiation under a clinical-supervision at an approximate interval of 2 hours.
